        "procedure": "Prepared with slight modifications of a literature method. Concentrated hydrogen peroxide (30%) was added to a saturated potassium carbonate solution. Cerium(III) chloride dissolved in bidistilled water was added dropwise with constant stirring. The orange mixture turned deep red at 60 °C. After rapid cooling to room temperature, hexaamminecobalt(III) chloride was added. Deep red crystals formed within a few days in a refrigerator.",
